WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.700
Step 1.

1.2
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.031
Select Settings in the facility sidebar, then Referral availability under Clinical.

1.3
00:00:06.031 --> 00:00:09.179
Every referral goes to one referral availability.

1.4
00:00:09.179 --> 00:00:14.753
It sets the referral forms and the team that Care assigns to each new referral.

2.1
00:00:14.753 --> 00:00:18.543
Step 2. Choose where the referral availability belongs.

2.2
00:00:18.543 --> 00:00:22.599
The page starts with the referral availability of the facility.

2.3
00:00:22.599 --> 00:00:27.604
For a department, select Filter, then the department under Department.

3.1
00:00:27.604 --> 00:00:32.850
Step 3. Select Add referral availability at the top right of the page.

3.2
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.704
Care opens the Add referral availability sheet.

4.1
00:00:36.704 --> 00:00:40.781
Step 4. Enter the Name and Description, choose the Status,

4.2
00:00:40.781 --> 00:00:43.882
and set Accept referrals from other facilities.

4.3
00:00:43.882 --> 00:00:49.317
Only an Active referral availability can receive new referrals.

5.1
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:54.125
Step 5. Under Referral forms, choose Request form or Response form,

5.2
00:00:54.125 --> 00:00:57.731
then select the questionnaire in Search active forms.

5.3
00:00:57.731 --> 00:01:00.792
A request form captures the referral details,

5.4
00:01:00.792 --> 00:01:05.306
and a response form captures the receiving team's findings.

6.1
00:01:05.306 --> 00:01:06.084
Step 6.

6.2
00:01:06.084 --> 00:01:11.964
Under Default care team, choose a person in Select Member and a role in Select

6.3
00:01:11.964 --> 00:01:22.422
Role, then select Add. Care assigns these people to each new referral.

7.1
00:01:22.422 --> 00:01:27.610
Step 7. Select Add referral availability at the bottom right of the sheet.

7.2
00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.347
Care shows Referral availability created,

7.3
00:01:30.347 --> 00:01:34.117
and the new referral availability is in the list.
